  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and preferring the lottery that is more left-skewed, i.e., one where more probability is assigned to favorable outcomes. The individual did consider outcomes and probabilities, which is necessary information, but they did not analyze or mention the shape of the distribution, concentration of probability on favorable outcomes, or skewness. Instead, they used expected value and personal utility/risk aversion as justification. There is no indication that they assessed which lottery has a greater probability mass on favorable outcomes. The justification is aligned with risk-averse expected utility reasoning, not skewness-based preference. Therefore, while some relevant data (outcomes and probabilities) were considered, the rule of the decision reason (preferring more left-skewed distributions) was not applied in the justification.",
